VIOLATION (meta-compliance) — the artifact inverts the contract it claims to express and fails the
authoring meta-rules on content while carrying every piece of the expected furniture.

SUBSTANTIVE INVERSION. verify-claims-before-write.md MUST-2(a) makes a claim carried from a design
document, a prior session or a handed-down framing PRESUMED FALSE until re-derived; this artifact
writes exactly those three sources in as grounds for restatement without re-derivation ("may
normally be restated ... because the establishing step already did the work"). MUST-2(b) forbids
citing a value read through truncated output; this artifact licenses sampling ("a representative
sample of it is usually sufficient ... may read the portion of the output that is convenient").
MUST-3 forbids relying on the structural backstops INSTEAD of verifying before the write; this
artifact makes that reliance the policy ("The release pipeline is the appropriate place for
surface errors to surface in any case ... an agent may reasonably rely on that"). Each is the
parent's DO-NOT stated as a DO.

AUTHORING DEFECTS, all of them content rather than absence. The section is headed "MUST Rules"
while the operative modals throughout are should / normally / generally / may / usually, so the
clause carries no modal force. The DO/DO-NOT block restates its own headings in prose instead of
showing two commands whose outcomes differ — nothing in it is runnable and nothing discriminates.
The BLOCKED list is abstract paraphrase of a disposition ("Being excessively thorough about
confirmation...") rather than matchable agent speech, so no rationalization an agent actually
utters would match it. The Why asserts budget cost and closes on "claims that have already been
established are mostly still true", which is the belief under test rather than the consequence of
breach.

NOT DEFECTS. The frontmatter, the Origin section, the Trust-Posture Wiring block with its
canonical field set, the single numbered clause heading, the Why line, the DO/DO-NOT block and the
BLOCKED heading are all PRESENT — the pole is surface-equalized with its counterpart and must not
be scored on missing furniture. The advisory severity in the Wiring block follows from the
inverted premise and is not a separate defect.
